      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# AuthFlow Authentication Module Documentation\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Introduction](#introduction)\n2. [Installation](#installation)\n3. [Configuration](#configuration)\n4. [Usage](#usage)\n5. [Error Handling](#error-handling)\n6. [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n7. [FAQs](#faqs)\n8. [Conclusion](#conclusion)\n\n## Introduction\nAuthFlow is an advanced authentication module designed to streamline user authentication processes in your applications. It supports various authentication methods, including OAuth, SAML, and custom tokens.\n\n## Installation\nTo install AuthFlow, run the following command in your project directory:\n```\nnpm install authflow\n```\n\n## Configuration\nAuthFlow can be configured by creating a configuration file `authflow-config.js` in your project root:\n```javascript\nconst authflowConfig = {\n  clientId: 'your-client-id',\n  clientSecret: 'your-client-secret',\n  redirectUri: 'your-redirect-uri',\n  scope: 'your-scope',\n  provider: 'your-provider',\n  // Add more configuration options as needed\n};\nmodule.exports = authflowConfig;\n```\n\n## Usage\nTo use AuthFlow",
      "source": "target",
