      "content": "# AuthFlow Authentication Module Documentation\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Introduction](#introduction)\n2. [Installation](#installation)\n   - [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)\n   - [Installation Command](#installation-command)\n3. [Configuration](#configuration)\n   - [Configuration File](#configuration-file)\n   - [Configuration Options](#configuration-options)\n4. [Usage](#usage)\n   - [Initialization](#initialization)\n   - [Authentication Methods](#authentication-methods)\n   - [Error Handling](#error-handling)\n5. [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n   - [Security](#security)\n   - [Performance](#performance)\n6. [FAQs](#faqs)\n7. [Conclusion](#conclusion)\n\n## Introduction\nAuthFlow is an advanced authentication module designed to streamline user authentication processes in your applications. It supports various authentication methods, including OAuth, SAML, and custom tokens.\n\n## Installation\nTo install AuthFlow, run the following command in your project directory:\n```\nnpm install authflow\n```\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Node.js and npm installed\n- Basic knowledge of JavaScript and Node.js\n\n### Installation Command",
